        "id": 105827,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-07T11:28:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yup, you can play any combination you like of hero, villain, and environment decks. It's just the Vengeance villains who are different, as they have a mechanic unique to them in which you fight H of them, as opposed to other villains where you just fight that villain. Okay, the Ennead are a bit different in that they're a villain group as well, but they only have the one deck between them and all act on the same turn (a Vengeance game has villain and hero turns alternating, so you normally have each player controlling the villain who predeces them), same as the Sentinels do.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:35:33.680Z",
